---
// Claim 3 · judgment does not delegate, it concentrates.
// Geometry: two-bars-shared-edge. The length difference is the whole claim;
// no scale, no percentage, nothing to calibrate.
---

<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 620 166" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
     role="img"
     aria-label="Two bars starting from the same left edge: the decisions a run makes on its own, each recorded with the criterion it used, run almost the full width; the three kinds that stop and wait for a person are a short segment beside them.">

  <!-- INVARIANT: both bars start at x=46. The length difference IS the claim.
       Do not add a scale, a legend or a percentage; the shared edge already
       makes the two lengths comparable. The short bar is not a measured
       ratio, it is the count of kinds: three, named below it. -->

  <g font-family="var(--fig-label-font, 'Fira Code', monospace)" font-size="11.5">

    <text x="46" y="36" fill="var(--fig-ink, currentColor)" opacity="0.85">decided without you, each with its criterion recorded</text>
    <line x1="46" y1="56" x2="574" y2="56"
          stroke="var(--fig-ink, currentColor)" stroke-width="9" opacity="0.26" stroke-linecap="round"/>

    <text x="46" y="102" fill="var(--fig-accent, #d4af37)">stops and waits for you</text>
    <line x1="46" y1="122" x2="146" y2="122"
          stroke="var(--fig-accent, #d4af37)" stroke-width="9" opacity="0.9" stroke-linecap="round"/>

    <g font-size="10.5" fill="var(--fig-accent, #d4af37)" opacity="0.85">
      <text x="46" y="150">a scope call</text>
      <text x="200" y="150">a fact only you know</text>
      <text x="404" y="150">an outward-facing effect</text>
    </g>
  </g>
</svg>
